WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.234 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Welcome to the show!

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.068 line:92%
-I am so happy to be here.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
-We're very happy to have you.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
We do not -- You are the first
Supreme Court Justice

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've ever had on the show
This a big deal for us.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.275 line:92%
-Well, I hope not the last

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:10.510 line:92%
-I hope not the last, too.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.479 size:81% position:41% line:92%
We've got eight to go.

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:13.279 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:17.050
I want to ask, having Suprem
Court Justice in a family.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.785
-Mm-hmm.
-Because obviously you have one,

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.153 line:92%
do people ever in your famil

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
ask you to rule
on disagreements?

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that something
that ever comes up?

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:24.791 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-They did once.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:25.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They did once.
How did that go --

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:29.162
Did they regret it in the en
that they asked you to rule?

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:29.796 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I regretted it.

00:00:29.796 --> 00:00:31.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You regretted it, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Nobody listened to me.
-Yeah.

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would say,
in an interfamily,

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
if there was ever a time t
recuse yourself, it would be -

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That would be it.
-Yeah, that would be the time.

00:00:39.639 --> 00:00:42.242
There are obviously a lot of
questions I'd love to ask yo

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
about things and goings-on
at the Supreme Court,

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you are not
in a position to answer them

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:52.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I am too stupid
to trick you into doing so

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:52.752 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you can -- you can tell us
about your book.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.323 line:92%
So tell us about the story

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.259 size:75% position:38%
and what brought you
to write this one.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.361 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, the story,

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.963 line:92%
and the line, "just ask,"

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:07.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
came from two separate
inspirations.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.637 line:92%
The writing of this kind of book

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:15.975
happened because the daughte
of a woman who worked with m

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:19.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
has an unusual
childhood condition.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.748 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And on occasion,

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:24.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
she would be sick
and would miss school

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
or activities
she wanted to engage in.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
And once, she was
very sad about that.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
sad about what she was
dealing with,

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:36.529 size:84% position:42%
sad about the things
she would miss in life.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.965 line:92%
And her mother, by happenstance,

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:43.603
read her a children's book
not written by me, but about me.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:47.207
At the end of reading it, sh
looked at her mother and said --

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, mind you, most 5-year-old
can't say my name.

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But her mom worked for me

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.379 line:92%
so she could say my name.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:58.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Justice Sotomayor,
she could do it with diabetes.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.687 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I can do it, too.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:03.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm gonna do
exactly what she did.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:08.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna to study hard
and not let this stop me."

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience "aww"s ]
She's now 12.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.431 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's wonderful.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:14.033 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:17.637 line:92%
-The story -- The story create

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.039 size:81% position:41% line:92%
two things in my mind.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:24.310
The first is that children
with difficult circumstances

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:29.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
like hearing
that other people have made it

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:33.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I knew there might be
some power to my story.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:36.623 line:92%
And so I first did a parent book

00:02:36.623 --> 00:02:41.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I told more details
about my life story

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:46.032
and my dealing with my diabetes,
among many other things.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I also knew
that I wanted to reach

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:54.574 size:78% position:39%
all of those children
that have conditions

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:58.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they deal with
every day of their lives.

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:02.248 size:88% position:44%
And just about everybody
knows a child like that,

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:07.287
whether it's something
like an allergy or asthma

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:09.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
or other things
that you can't see --

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
autism, attention deficit,
Down syndrome,

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.396 line:92%
some of those you can see.

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:19.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
But there are
so many kids out there

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:24.204 line:92%
who every day live with courag

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:28.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
and who add so much
to the quality of our living

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:31.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I wanted to be
a voice for them.

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:35.148 line:92%
So I wanted to write a book,

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:39.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the title
and how it came to life

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:43.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
was something that had happene
to me over 30 years ago.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's so wonderful
you did that.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:46.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
And obviously, you have
such a unique story

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:50.396 size:78% position:39%
among the many things
that are unique --

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.264 line:92%
First Hispanic on the court.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:54.334
And obviously, there have no
been a lot of women on the court

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.501 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
over the years.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.070 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.172 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You're also --

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.108 size:88% position:44%
I mean, most importantly
for us here in the city,

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:03.676 size:81% position:41% line:92%
you're from the Bronx.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That helps.
-That helps.

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:08.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- And while I do not
find this --

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:11.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
As a Red Sox fan, I find i
very distressing that you're -

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.786 line:92%
-Ooh, I liked you until that

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:14.420 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, well...

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, how do you think I fel
when I saw this photo?

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.492 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:20.593 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You know --

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.262 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:25.999
-And it's nice.
Couple of judges from the Bronx.

